00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:18.780
Disappointing Person

00:02:18.780 --> 00:02:22.210
What do you mean you forgot to get gas?
Disappointing Person

00:02:22.210 --> 00:02:22.230
What do you mean you forgot to get gas?

00:02:22.230 --> 00:02:25.010
Well, usually my dad or Masami gets it...

00:02:25.010 --> 00:02:28.930
This is my older brother's, so...

00:02:28.930 --> 00:02:33.360
You're ridiculous. What idiot gave you a license?

00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:36.150
At least I <i>have </i>a license...

00:02:36.700 --> 00:02:39.070
Chi, did you borrow a bike too?

00:02:39.070 --> 00:02:40.780
This is Momiyama's.

00:02:41.520 --> 00:02:43.150
Momiyama?

00:02:47.030 --> 00:02:50.070
They're really attached to her, huh?

00:02:50.070 --> 00:02:53.190
I wish I had a scooter...
Pushing <i>that </i>would be a breeze.

00:02:54.760 --> 00:02:56.700
We've got a long way to go...

00:03:00.430 --> 00:03:02.920
Th-Thank you. How much do I owe you?

00:03:02.920 --> 00:03:04.100
Don't worry about it.

00:03:04.100 --> 00:03:06.470
Huh? Why? Too cute to pay?

00:03:06.470 --> 00:03:07.890
No.

00:03:08.270 --> 00:03:10.390
It's part of my friendship project.

00:03:11.230 --> 00:03:13.470
Mie Motors?

00:03:13.470 --> 00:03:14.520
I see.

00:03:18.470 --> 00:03:19.980
Well then, if you'll excuse me.

00:03:23.230 --> 00:03:24.860
So fast...

00:03:35.270 --> 00:03:38.190
Daddy, I'm home.

00:03:39.780 --> 00:03:41.380
Have you been well?

00:03:42.630 --> 00:03:46.230
Sorry I haven't called in a while.

00:03:49.230 --> 00:03:51.210
See? It <i>is</i> Hime.

00:03:51.210 --> 00:03:52.870
Welcome home!

00:03:52.870 --> 00:03:54.450
You've gotten so big!

00:03:54.450 --> 00:03:56.340
Have you been well, Himeko?

00:03:56.340 --> 00:03:58.600
L-Long time no see.

00:03:59.100 --> 00:04:01.110
Isn't this great, Mamoru?

00:04:02.520 --> 00:04:05.230
Daddy, um...

00:04:05.230 --> 00:04:07.520
There's something I want you to look at.

00:04:09.140 --> 00:04:12.100
Mamoru, talk to the poor girl!

00:04:12.100 --> 00:04:14.980
Your little girl's finally returned.

00:04:14.980 --> 00:04:17.180
It's been what, three, four years?

00:04:17.180 --> 00:04:20.700
Mamoru, Hime's turned into a real beauty!

00:04:20.700 --> 00:04:22.430
That's not true.

00:04:23.250 --> 00:04:25.700
Jeez, you stubborn old man.

00:04:25.700 --> 00:04:28.230
He's too proud to turn this way, you know.

00:04:28.230 --> 00:04:30.380
Well, this isn't gonna be easy.

00:04:30.380 --> 00:04:33.430
Hey, Hime. Why don't you come by my house for some tea first?

00:04:33.430 --> 00:04:36.060
No, come to my house! You can relax there.

00:04:36.060 --> 00:04:38.700
It's just across the street! She can even sleep over.

00:04:38.700 --> 00:04:41.100
Idiot. Do you think we'd let a young woman spend the night at a widower's house?

00:04:41.100 --> 00:04:43.030
Hey, Daddy, it's this...
Idiot. Do you think we'd let a young woman spend the night at a widower's house?

00:04:43.030 --> 00:04:43.900
Mamoru's a widower too.
Hey, Daddy, it's this...

00:04:43.900 --> 00:04:44.820
Mamoru's a widower too.

00:04:45.120 --> 00:04:47.250
He's also her dad!

00:04:47.250 --> 00:04:50.070
Well, I'm like a big brother.
Right, Hime? Am I right?

00:04:50.070 --> 00:04:51.570
Lemme help ya!

00:04:52.210 --> 00:04:55.830
Silence!

00:05:04.470 --> 00:05:05.940
Daddy!

00:05:17.450 --> 00:05:18.640
He said it's dangerous.

00:05:24.900 --> 00:05:26.380
Wh-What is this?

00:05:26.380 --> 00:05:27.450
A dorsal fin?

00:05:27.450 --> 00:05:29.780
A shachihoko, I think?

00:05:29.780 --> 00:05:32.950
Why would something like that fall from the sky?

00:05:32.950 --> 00:05:33.810
Golden Shachi General Hospital
Golden Shachi General Hospital

00:05:33.810 --> 00:05:34.820
I'm glad you weren't seriously injured.
Golden Shachi General Hospital
Golden Shachi General Hospital

00:05:34.820 --> 00:05:37.100
I'm glad you weren't seriously injured.

00:05:37.650 --> 00:05:38.760
The others okay?

00:05:38.760 --> 00:05:41.960
Just some scratches, thanks to you.

00:05:42.700 --> 00:05:45.940
Right now, Uncle Kokichi and the others are fixing the workshop.

00:05:45.940 --> 00:05:48.080
Oh, and the kiln is fine.

00:05:48.760 --> 00:05:52.720
The shachihoko around town were all broken, though.

00:05:53.270 --> 00:05:55.140
Not even the castle's golden one was spared.

00:05:56.960 --> 00:06:00.060
I wonder if the people from Mie did it.

00:06:00.700 --> 00:06:02.310
Who knows?

00:06:03.610 --> 00:06:06.100
Didn't you have something you wanted to tell me?

00:06:06.100 --> 00:06:08.020
Hm? Oh...

00:06:09.700 --> 00:06:11.280
Forget it.

00:06:12.810 --> 00:06:15.210
Oh right, why don't I buy some coffee?

00:06:15.210 --> 00:06:17.560
Is the owner of Mach-ountain doing well?

00:06:17.560 --> 00:06:19.810
I haven't seen him in a while, so I'll go—

00:06:19.810 --> 00:06:22.030
Hey wait, what are you doing?

00:06:22.030 --> 00:06:23.290
I'm going home.

00:06:23.290 --> 00:06:25.740
But the doctor wanted you to stay overnight!

00:06:25.740 --> 00:06:28.290
I have a deadline approaching.

00:06:28.650 --> 00:06:29.870
A deadline?

00:06:29.870 --> 00:06:32.120
For a shachihoko, of course.

00:06:32.120 --> 00:06:35.900
The golden shachi on the castle needs to be remade too.

00:06:39.810 --> 00:06:41.360
You're right.

00:06:41.360 --> 00:06:44.670
It's been a while since I've seen them.

00:06:44.670 --> 00:06:46.020
They sure are amazing.

00:06:47.070 --> 00:06:47.770
Himeko.

00:06:47.770 --> 00:06:49.010
What is it?

00:06:50.540 --> 00:06:52.520
Oh, never mind.

00:06:54.810 --> 00:06:56.070
All right, here.

00:06:56.580 --> 00:07:01.580
There're a ton o' people here fer th' Tenmusu Grand Prix this weekend, so you be careful, ya hear?

00:07:02.450 --> 00:07:03.580
What'sa matter?

00:07:03.580 --> 00:07:05.650
N-Nothing...

00:07:05.650 --> 00:07:10.610
There's also that big hullabaloo what with all the shachihoko bein' blown ta bits,

00:07:10.610 --> 00:07:13.170
so the folks of old Aichi're all a bit on edge.

00:07:13.500 --> 00:07:14.780
Like that thing earlier?

00:07:14.780 --> 00:07:16.380
More bombs?

00:07:16.380 --> 00:07:19.410
Make sure ya don't hang around the vigilante HQs

00:07:19.410 --> 00:07:22.810
o' them Aichi Tenmusus and Mie Motors.

00:07:30.870 --> 00:07:33.440
Welcome!

00:07:36.870 --> 00:07:38.450
That's a strange rule.

00:07:38.900 --> 00:07:41.580
Forced to visit a restaurant if they hit us with food...

00:07:41.580 --> 00:07:43.950
The competition for customers is fierce.

00:07:44.340 --> 00:07:46.460
It's fine since we were hungry, though!

00:07:46.960 --> 00:07:49.160
Yo Boss, hit me up with another tenmusu!

00:07:49.160 --> 00:07:50.810
I'd like miso cutlets!

00:07:50.810 --> 00:07:52.010
Red bean toast...

00:07:52.010 --> 00:07:53.460
Takoyaki, please!

00:07:56.920 --> 00:07:59.180
Hey, that's my parfait!

00:07:59.470 --> 00:08:02.260
Huh? Oh, s'rry!

00:08:02.260 --> 00:08:04.140
"S'rry" isn't gonna cut it!

00:08:04.140 --> 00:08:08.030
Aw, come on! My hand moved on its own!

00:08:08.030 --> 00:08:09.690
Hey, that's my red bean spaghetti!

00:08:10.360 --> 00:08:10.940
S'rry.

00:08:21.610 --> 00:08:23.940
Did you come to see the Tenmusu Grand Prix?

00:08:23.940 --> 00:08:26.270
Oh, no...

00:08:26.270 --> 00:08:29.960
We're looking for where a person called Uotora Himeko lives.

00:08:30.450 --> 00:08:31.500
Himeko.

00:08:31.500 --> 00:08:32.300
Huh?

00:08:32.300 --> 00:08:33.880
They're here for you.

00:08:34.460 --> 00:08:35.430
Old Mie, Old Aichi
Uotora Himeko

00:08:35.430 --> 00:08:36.630
I don't know anything about this, though.
Old Mie, Old Aichi
Uotora Himeko

00:08:36.630 --> 00:08:37.500
I don't know anything about this, though.

00:08:37.500 --> 00:08:39.140
Huh? But...

00:08:40.870 --> 00:08:41.840
Wait,

00:08:41.840 --> 00:08:44.920
have you been to Tokorozawa?

00:08:44.920 --> 00:08:45.850
Huh?

00:08:47.960 --> 00:08:49.440
One, two!

00:08:50.960 --> 00:08:52.720
Are you all right, Nozomi?!

00:08:52.720 --> 00:08:55.940
Masami, gimme your Moonlight Stone for a sec!

00:08:58.940 --> 00:09:00.360
Um...

00:09:01.980 --> 00:09:03.140
Can you...

00:09:10.830 --> 00:09:12.650
It's fine. Let me see it.

00:09:23.960 --> 00:09:27.560
Did that stone fall from the sky?

00:09:28.100 --> 00:09:30.500
Yeah! It's the Moonlight Stone.

00:09:30.500 --> 00:09:33.440
"Moonlight Stone", huh? That's cute.

00:09:34.100 --> 00:09:35.230
Ta-da!

00:09:36.430 --> 00:09:38.980
Mine is the "Star of the Circuit".

00:09:38.980 --> 00:09:41.740
When I see this stone, I can do my best!

00:09:43.960 --> 00:09:48.030
Oh, that was you? You've gotten big!

00:09:48.030 --> 00:09:51.380
Masami was super happy with that.

00:09:51.380 --> 00:09:53.120
Thank you very much!

00:09:53.120 --> 00:09:54.370
I'm glad she liked it!

00:09:54.370 --> 00:09:54.870
Dear Maccha Green,
Peacebroker of Tokorozawa
Please excuse the sudden letter.
I'll get straight to the point.
Please help bring peace to Mie-Aichi.
We need your strength.
As payment, I will give you
my precious stone.

00:09:54.870 --> 00:09:57.380
Oh, but this isn't me.
Dear Maccha Green,
Peacebroker of Tokorozawa
Please excuse the sudden letter.
I'll get straight to the point.
Please help bring peace to Mie-Aichi.
We need your strength.
As payment, I will give you
my precious stone.

00:09:57.380 --> 00:09:59.320
I've been traveling all over the place,

00:09:59.320 --> 00:10:02.100
and I've never heard of this Maccha Green.

00:10:02.100 --> 00:10:04.320
Oh, actually it's Masami...

00:10:04.320 --> 00:10:08.900
Hey, is your precious stone that Circuit thing?

00:10:08.900 --> 00:10:10.700
I told you, I don't know what that's about.

00:10:10.700 --> 00:10:12.600
I can't part with it.

00:10:12.600 --> 00:10:15.350
It isn't mine.

00:10:16.360 --> 00:10:17.720
Huh?

00:10:17.720 --> 00:10:20.450
Sorry, but I have bigger problems.

00:10:21.610 --> 00:10:24.560
Hey, you can't do that!

00:10:24.560 --> 00:10:26.870
Are you... stress eating?

00:10:27.160 --> 00:10:28.990
Yeah, that's how it is.

00:10:31.620 --> 00:10:33.750
D-Dandy, sir!

00:10:42.170 --> 00:10:44.170
What's the meaning of this, Dandy?!
What's the meaning of this, Dandy?!

00:10:44.540 --> 00:10:45.800
What are you talking about?

00:10:46.050 --> 00:10:50.390
We, the Mie Motors, are getting
blamed for the shachi bombing!

00:10:50.680 --> 00:10:52.930
You Aichi Tenmusus are the ones
spreading these lies, aren't you?

00:10:52.930 --> 00:10:54.600
How absurd.

00:10:54.640 --> 00:10:56.060
That's our line!

00:10:57.560 --> 00:11:01.400
In accordance with the Twin Tower Declaration,
I challenge you to a duel!

00:11:01.530 --> 00:11:04.320
It's about time we establish the Mie
as the rightful rulers of this land!

00:11:05.320 --> 00:11:06.700
A duel, huh?

00:11:06.700 --> 00:11:08.680
Oh, please, wait!

00:11:08.680 --> 00:11:09.200
Nonsuke!
Nozomi!

00:11:09.200 --> 00:11:10.450
Th-That's dange—

00:11:10.450 --> 00:11:15.580
We're peacebrokers who have come from Tokorozawa in Maccha Green's place.

00:11:15.580 --> 00:11:18.210
Please don't fight with the people of Aichi!

00:11:18.810 --> 00:11:20.710
This is a little too dangerous for you.

00:11:20.840 --> 00:11:24.840
Maccha from Tokorozawa?!
We at Mie Motors are the real experts at "mach"-a!

00:11:28.850 --> 00:11:31.720
Your challenge is invalid, Vice Captain.

00:11:31.720 --> 00:11:32.600
What?

00:11:32.600 --> 00:11:40.480
The Twin Tower Declaration allows for vigilante squad captains to agree to an <i>honorable</i> fight.

00:11:40.760 --> 00:11:42.810
You are not the captain of the Mie Motors.

00:11:42.810 --> 00:11:47.270
In addition, you have taunted and frightened a peacemaker who came from afar.

00:11:47.270 --> 00:11:49.360
<i>Honorable</i>, you are not.

00:11:49.360 --> 00:11:53.120
Therefore, I will never accept a duel with you.

00:11:53.410 --> 00:11:54.520
He's so dandy.

00:11:54.520 --> 00:11:56.120
Yes, he is.

00:11:56.250 --> 00:11:59.670
Whatever. You're just as dandy as always!

00:12:00.040 --> 00:12:03.130
Just you wait! Your dandy days
are numbered, mark my words!

00:12:08.140 --> 00:12:10.220
Those guys think they own the place!

00:12:10.670 --> 00:12:12.070
I can't take it anymore!

00:12:12.070 --> 00:12:13.410
Let's put an end to this!

00:12:13.410 --> 00:12:16.070
I'm sure they're the ones who broke the shachihoko.

00:12:16.070 --> 00:12:17.740
We can't say that for sure yet.

00:12:17.740 --> 00:12:18.560
But—

00:12:18.560 --> 00:12:21.700
How can you still be so dandy?

00:12:22.300 --> 00:12:26.280
Do you really want one of us to take over the other?

00:12:26.560 --> 00:12:27.960
Is that it?

00:12:29.700 --> 00:12:33.650
I heard that the captain of Mie Motors wishes for reconciliation.

00:12:33.650 --> 00:12:37.290
He's changing the organization from the inside, and leading the residents of Mie to—

00:12:37.290 --> 00:12:38.610
We can't wait for that!

00:12:38.610 --> 00:12:40.040
Let's decide it with a race!

00:12:40.040 --> 00:12:41.230
I will race!

00:12:41.230 --> 00:12:42.030
No, I will!

00:12:42.030 --> 00:12:43.380
Please let me do it!

00:12:43.380 --> 00:12:44.170
I will!

00:12:44.170 --> 00:12:45.300
Captain.

00:12:45.300 --> 00:12:46.670
Captain!

00:12:59.670 --> 00:13:02.380
Himeko, do you do any racing?

00:13:02.380 --> 00:13:06.220
Huh? No, not at all. Why?

00:13:06.630 --> 00:13:09.920
Your stone's name is "Star of the Circuit"...

00:13:09.920 --> 00:13:12.430
Oh... that's...

00:13:14.380 --> 00:13:17.230
We'll be heading back to Mr Dandy's cafe now.

00:13:17.230 --> 00:13:19.360
We have to fix that too.

00:13:19.360 --> 00:13:20.860
You guys are going to help?

00:13:21.230 --> 00:13:24.630
He's letting us stay in a spare room at the cafe,

00:13:24.630 --> 00:13:27.010
so we thought we'd at least help out in return.

00:13:27.010 --> 00:13:29.120
Oh, are you Hime's friends?

00:13:29.670 --> 00:13:31.050
Come in and rest a bit.

00:13:32.470 --> 00:13:35.740
If we could at least decide on the name of the country...

00:13:36.850 --> 00:13:38.760
It's still unnamed?

00:13:38.760 --> 00:13:43.210
We couldn't stop arguing over whether it should be "Aichi-Mie" or "Mie-Aichi".

00:13:43.210 --> 00:13:45.760
We can't give them an inch on this.

00:13:45.760 --> 00:13:50.850
Those guys are trying to make us feel guilty.

00:13:50.850 --> 00:13:53.670
We can't have them doing whatever they want with the name, either!

00:13:53.670 --> 00:13:54.770
Guilty?

00:13:54.770 --> 00:13:57.500
We were fighting over the roots of tenmusu and miso cutlets.

00:13:57.500 --> 00:13:59.030
That's why merging came up.

00:13:59.580 --> 00:14:02.030
It was better than continuing to fight between us.

00:14:02.030 --> 00:14:06.650
Actually, both have their origins in Mie,
so Aichi compromised on a number of things,

00:14:06.650 --> 00:14:09.000
like having the public roads be a race circuit.

00:14:09.000 --> 00:14:13.870
They may have thought of it, but we put our spin on it and made it famous!

00:14:13.870 --> 00:14:17.100
If Mie's the inventor, then we're the birthplace!

00:14:17.100 --> 00:14:18.760
You got that right, Kokichi.

00:14:19.110 --> 00:14:21.120
They just don't get it.

00:14:21.120 --> 00:14:23.340
Right, Ichizo? Right?

00:14:23.340 --> 00:14:28.160
Even if that's the case, Mr. Dandy and the vigilante squad are dealing with it.

00:14:28.160 --> 00:14:32.300
Before we start pointing fingers, we should fix the shachihoko.

00:14:32.300 --> 00:14:35.110
We'll show them there's no use in breaking them.

00:14:35.110 --> 00:14:38.400
First is the golden shachi at the castle. Right, Mamoru?

00:14:40.060 --> 00:14:41.520
Mamoru?

00:14:42.360 --> 00:14:44.410
It looks like that might be difficult.

00:14:44.410 --> 00:14:45.270
Huh?

00:14:45.270 --> 00:14:46.480
Why?

00:14:47.380 --> 00:14:49.360
It looks like my arm's done for.

00:14:49.360 --> 00:14:50.500
What did you say?

00:14:51.320 --> 00:14:55.100
Actually, I've had a strange numbness for a while.

00:14:55.100 --> 00:14:57.560
I've made do until now,

00:14:57.560 --> 00:15:01.970
but it looks like I've lost feeling in it,
and it won't do what I want it to anymore.

00:15:02.360 --> 00:15:05.260
Then, what about the broken shachihoko?

00:15:05.520 --> 00:15:08.430
What, <i>indeed</i>...

00:15:08.430 --> 00:15:10.650
Here, let me have a look.

00:15:10.650 --> 00:15:13.700
You sure your arm didn't just fall asleep?

00:15:16.270 --> 00:15:18.650
You make it, Himeko.

00:15:18.650 --> 00:15:19.300
Huh?

00:15:19.300 --> 00:15:21.940
Yeah, you're the only one who can!

00:15:21.940 --> 00:15:27.120
The Uotora carpenters have been making the Nagoya Castle shachihoko for generations.

00:15:27.120 --> 00:15:28.870
W-Wait a minute!

00:15:28.870 --> 00:15:31.900
Isn't this what the past five years of training were for?

00:15:31.900 --> 00:15:33.010
You can do it!

00:15:33.010 --> 00:15:34.160
I'm not who you think I am!

00:15:34.870 --> 00:15:38.120
I left because I hate those fish.

00:15:38.120 --> 00:15:39.700
I left to have fun.

00:15:39.700 --> 00:15:42.460
It got boring, so I came home.

00:15:42.900 --> 00:15:45.320
Besides, shachihoko are so weird.

00:15:45.320 --> 00:15:47.050
They're ugly little freaks.

00:15:47.630 --> 00:15:49.560
Why do they even curl like that?

00:15:52.740 --> 00:15:54.650
Look, let's see a doctor in the morning.

00:16:02.210 --> 00:16:04.360
Nozomi, we should go home soon—

00:16:04.360 --> 00:16:08.700
Um, is there anything we can do?

00:16:09.120 --> 00:16:09.200
Uotora Himeko
Dear Maccha Green,
Peacebroker of Tokorozawa
Please excuse the sudden letter.
I'll get straight to the point.
We received this with Himeko's name on it.

00:16:09.200 --> 00:16:12.200
We received this with Himeko's name on it.

00:16:12.200 --> 00:16:15.560
"Please help bring peace to Mie-Aichi"?

00:16:15.560 --> 00:16:16.850
Shouldn't it be Aichi-Mie?

00:16:16.850 --> 00:16:18.630
Himeko sent this?

00:16:18.630 --> 00:16:21.340
No, Himeko said she didn't know anything about it.

00:16:21.340 --> 00:16:23.000
Oh, that?

00:16:23.000 --> 00:16:23.780
Huh?

00:16:23.780 --> 00:16:25.610
Did you send this, Mamoru?

00:16:25.610 --> 00:16:26.940
No.

00:16:26.940 --> 00:16:30.090
Are you the Maccha-something-or-other from Tokorozawa?

00:16:30.670 --> 00:16:32.830
No, I'm here in her place.

00:16:32.830 --> 00:16:34.850
My name is Moritomo Nozomi.

00:16:34.850 --> 00:16:36.600
I'm Kosaka Yukina.

00:16:36.600 --> 00:16:38.160
I see.

00:16:38.160 --> 00:16:43.160
Then you should look for a guy running a bike taxi service tomorrow.

00:16:43.160 --> 00:16:45.300
He's the only one. Can't miss him.

00:16:45.300 --> 00:16:47.050
Bike taxi?

00:16:47.050 --> 00:16:48.570
What the heck is that?

00:16:49.580 --> 00:16:51.340
Suzuka Tomoki.

00:16:52.120 --> 00:16:54.740
The captain of the Mie Motors.

00:16:58.360 --> 00:17:00.960
Feel free to use the back room.

00:17:00.960 --> 00:17:04.940
Thanks! Wait, Mr Dandy, you don't live here?

00:17:04.940 --> 00:17:08.180
My home is somewhere else. It's just a small place, though.

00:17:08.180 --> 00:17:09.340
I see.

00:17:09.760 --> 00:17:13.630
Hey, so do you have one of those stones?

00:17:13.630 --> 00:17:14.600
Stones?

00:17:14.600 --> 00:17:19.980
You know, the stones Nozomi and that girl were talking about. The pink ones.

00:17:19.980 --> 00:17:21.480
I do not have one.

00:17:21.480 --> 00:17:26.740
Oh, come on. There can't be that many Bests who can exchange blows with a motorcycle.

00:17:26.740 --> 00:17:28.140
Let me see it!

00:17:28.140 --> 00:17:31.660
Oh, does that mean that girl is amazing, too?

00:17:32.070 --> 00:17:33.320
Himeko?

00:17:37.180 --> 00:17:41.210
Yeah, that girl might be amazing.

00:17:41.210 --> 00:17:45.460
Damn, I guess that stone really is amazing!

00:17:46.100 --> 00:17:47.530
Well, see you tomorrow.

00:17:47.530 --> 00:17:50.100
Oh, can you put that in the fridge?

00:17:50.100 --> 00:17:51.380
Oh, sure.

00:17:51.380 --> 00:17:53.480
Good night!

00:17:54.100 --> 00:17:58.230
What a jerk. It's not like I'm gonna <i>steal</i> it...

00:17:58.230 --> 00:18:00.640
That Dandy is stingier than he looks.

00:18:01.070 --> 00:18:02.600
Right, Chi?

00:18:04.140 --> 00:18:05.050
Huh?

00:18:09.030 --> 00:18:12.530
Probably somewhere being a little shutterbug again.

00:18:36.300 --> 00:18:37.250
I knew it.

00:18:38.430 --> 00:18:41.810
You lied about not being able to move your hand, didn't you?

00:18:42.520 --> 00:18:43.850
What are you trying to do?

00:18:45.030 --> 00:18:48.820
Were you pretending to be injured so you could force me to make the shachihoko?

00:18:49.320 --> 00:18:55.240
Because I won't take over Uotora unless you can't continue anymore?

00:18:56.960 --> 00:19:00.040
It's not like I'll ever be as good as you.

00:19:00.560 --> 00:19:05.680
No matter how many years I'm away to train, I'll never amount to much.

00:19:06.610 --> 00:19:07.360
Himeko.

00:19:07.360 --> 00:19:10.210
I wish all the shachihoko would just go away!

00:19:21.160 --> 00:19:22.480
Wait, Hime—

00:19:26.360 --> 00:19:27.810
Huh? Ai?

00:19:28.230 --> 00:19:29.470
What's the matter?

00:19:29.470 --> 00:19:31.940
Oh, Chi's...

00:19:36.670 --> 00:19:38.570
Bike taxi...

00:19:39.100 --> 00:19:40.830
Isn't that—

00:19:46.210 --> 00:19:50.840
There you are! I can't believe you ditched
the gang to work for charity!

00:19:51.250 --> 00:19:52.880
You guys should try it out some time, too.

00:19:52.880 --> 00:19:54.470
Who the hell has time for that?!

00:19:54.720 --> 00:19:57.260
We're being blamed for the Shachi bombings!

00:19:57.740 --> 00:20:01.600
What, really? I <i>thought</i> things seemed different around here...

00:20:02.140 --> 00:20:02.180
bike race will govern this country
The vigilante squad that wins the

00:20:02.220 --> 00:20:02.270
bike race will govern this country
The vigilante squad that wins the

00:20:02.390 --> 00:20:04.140
I need you to sign this proposal!

00:20:04.560 --> 00:20:07.100
I'll turn this situation around and
let Mie take the throne!

00:20:07.410 --> 00:20:11.150
No. Didn't I tell you to get along with old Aichi?

00:20:11.150 --> 00:20:12.440
This is your problem too, you know!

00:20:12.530 --> 00:20:14.780
We've gotta end this once and for all!

00:20:14.780 --> 00:20:18.610
I have a plan, so just wait a little longer.

00:20:18.870 --> 00:20:20.450
You have a plan now, do you?

00:20:20.660 --> 00:20:23.370
Let me guess, you called over some
nosy brats from somewhere else?

00:20:23.370 --> 00:20:24.370
Huh?

00:20:24.370 --> 00:20:26.370
And you call yourself a vigilante squad captain?!

00:20:27.000 --> 00:20:28.700
Well, what else can I do?

00:20:28.700 --> 00:20:31.630
I'm not captain material anyway.

00:20:31.920 --> 00:20:32.900
The title comes with being the fastest one out there!
Captain?

00:20:32.900 --> 00:20:34.420
He must be the person who sent the request, Suzuka Tomoki.
The title comes with being the fastest one out there!

00:20:34.420 --> 00:20:36.100
He must be the person who sent the request, Suzuka Tomoki.

00:20:36.100 --> 00:20:37.880
Really?

00:20:38.340 --> 00:20:41.720
That's not why I race.

00:20:42.070 --> 00:20:46.640
I just like racing and competing with fast guys.

00:20:47.270 --> 00:20:49.100
I'm sick of your pussy talk.

00:20:49.520 --> 00:20:52.820
Just sign the damn thing, and we'll
sort this out on our own.

00:20:52.980 --> 00:20:54.530
You don't have a problem if we just race them, right?

00:20:54.870 --> 00:20:56.530
Is that going to bring peace?

00:20:56.940 --> 00:20:58.650
Hell yeah, why wouldn't it?

00:21:01.670 --> 00:21:04.410
No. I can't give permission for that.

00:21:05.410 --> 00:21:06.160
Hold it!

00:21:12.420 --> 00:21:14.420
Shit, he's too fast!

00:21:18.900 --> 00:21:21.030
Found you, Suzuka Tomoki.

00:21:21.030 --> 00:21:23.720
Give your permission for a decisive battle as captain of the Mie Motors!

00:21:23.720 --> 00:21:25.720
And then race us!

00:21:31.760 --> 00:21:35.110
Then, we'll take these guys on first!

00:21:35.230 --> 00:21:37.030
Let's rock'n'roll, boys!

00:21:48.610 --> 00:21:51.160
That's the guardian god of the new country.

00:21:51.160 --> 00:21:52.560
Guardian god?

00:21:52.560 --> 00:21:53.420
That's right.

00:21:53.810 --> 00:21:59.120
Shachihoko used to protect houses from fire with the water from their mouths.

00:21:59.120 --> 00:22:02.930
If that's put up there where everyone can see, then this country will be peaceful and safe.

00:22:03.700 --> 00:22:05.280
A guardian god...

00:22:06.180 --> 00:22:07.930
Daddy, you're amazing!

00:22:08.300 --> 00:22:10.360
I'm gonna make shachihoko too!

00:22:10.360 --> 00:22:10.980
Really?

00:22:10.980 --> 00:22:13.100
I'm gonna be just like you!

00:22:45.270 --> 00:22:47.560
Tomoki?

00:22:48.180 --> 00:22:49.210
Hey.

00:23:12.290 --> 00:23:17.470
Thou shalt not pass

00:23:17.760 --> 00:23:22.850
Laws, reason, nobody is getting past

00:23:23.180 --> 00:23:28.680
I don't care what you say

00:23:28.680 --> 00:23:34.150
I'm not letting friends and lovers in either

00:23:34.860 --> 00:23:38.280
My only companion

00:23:39.610 --> 00:23:44.030
is the faint moonlight

00:23:45.120 --> 00:23:55.960
I'm now sitting in the cockpit

00:23:55.960 --> 00:24:02.220
of the black shadow

00:24:02.220 --> 00:24:05.850
deep in the white moon

